       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Sertraline's maximum recommended adult dose is 200 mg per day. An order for 1000 mg is five times that. It risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac effects such as QT prolongation. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg.\n\n2. **You're not a prescriber.** Medication orders should come from, or be verified by, a licensed clinician who is treating the patient. I can't confirm that this order was actually written by one.\n\nIf the order is real, please ask the prescribing clinician to confirm the intended dose. Sertraline is typically started at 25\u201350 mg once daily and goes up to 200 mg per day at most. Once I have a confirmed dose within the usual range, ideally from the clinician directly, I can enter it."
      }
